==== Gödel-Schmidt ====
Suppose that the “only thing we know about Godel” is that he is the author
of the Gödel's theorem. But suppose also that another German in fact wrote that
theorem but Gödel somehow successfully stole the credit. We all believe that
Gödel wrote the theorem and the only description *most of us can provide*


This is really a specific version of a more general problem. If we know the
meaning of “Gödel” or “Superman” or “Scott” or of any of the names of
external objects whose existence we can doubt, or be mistaken about – the objects
we only know and can refer to “by description” – then why can't we all provide
the definite descriptions on request?

it appears we must since we use the sentences correctly)

